---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import SectionNav from '../components/SectionNav.astro';

const sections = [
  { href: '#challenge', label: 'Challenge' },
  { href: '#brief', label: 'Design brief' },
  { href: '#mechanism', label: 'Mechanism' },
  { href: '#cartridge', label: 'Cartridge' },
  { href: '#boundaries', label: 'Boundaries' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Project design" description="Explore AquaSense's problem framing, cell-free sensing architecture, closed cartridge, and responsible-use boundaries.">
  <PageHero index="01" eyebrow="Project design" title="A screening tool built around the decision." lead="AquaSense is a conceptual, cell-free biosensor for preliminary lead screening. The molecular circuit matters—but so do the enclosure, instructions, and next step." />

  <div class="page-shell">
    <SectionNav items={sections} />
    <article class="page-content">
      <section id="challenge" data-reveal>
        <div class="prose">
          <p class="eyebrow">01 · Challenge</p>
          <h2>Detection is only useful when it leads somewhere.</h2>
          <p>Water-quality testing often involves a chain of collection, transport, laboratory analysis, interpretation, and communication. Each handoff adds time and can make preliminary investigation harder in remote or resource-constrained settings.</p>
          <p>AquaSense focuses on the earliest decision in that chain: <strong>does this sample warrant prioritized confirmatory testing?</strong> It is deliberately framed as a screening concept rather than a replacement for accredited laboratory methods.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="challenge-map" role="img" aria-label="Comparison between the existing testing journey and the AquaSense concept">
          <div><span class="mono">Existing journey</span><b>Collect</b><i></i><b>Transport</b><i></i><b>Analyze</b><i></i><b>Interpret</b></div>
          <div><span class="mono">AquaSense concept</span><b>Collect</b><i></i><b>Screen locally</b><i></i><b>Prioritize follow-up</b></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="brief" data-reveal>
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">02 · Design brief</p>
          <h2>Requirements before features.</h2>
          <p>The brief translates stakeholder needs into criteria that can be tested. A compelling technology that fails the context is still a failed design.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="requirement-grid">
          <article class="requirement"><span>R—01</span><h3>Legible</h3><p>Use three named result bands and plain-language actions, never color alone.</p><b>Accessibility</b></article>
          <article class="requirement"><span>R—02</span><h3>Contained</h3><p>Keep the reaction sealed and use a cell-free system to avoid environmental release.</p><b>Biosafety</b></article>
          <article class="requirement"><span>R—03</span><h3>Portable</h3><p>Operate without specialized readers or a continuous power supply.</p><b>Field use</b></article>
          <article class="requirement"><span>R—04</span><h3>Honest</h3><p>State uncertainty, interferences, and the need for laboratory confirmation.</p><b>Trust</b></article>
          <article class="requirement"><span>R—05</span><h3>Traceable</h3><p>Give each cartridge a sample ID and a durable place to record context.</p><b>Documentation</b></article>
          <article class="requirement"><span>R—06</span><h3>Actionable</h3><p>Connect each output to a next step defined with local partners.</p><b>Implementation</b></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="mechanism" data-reveal>
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">03 · Proposed mechanism</p>
          <h2>Recognition, then translation.</h2>
          <p>The proposed architecture separates the molecular event from the interface that communicates it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mechanism-figure" role="img" aria-label="Conceptual sensing pathway from lead ions through a regulatory switch to a visible reporter">
          <div class="m-node ions"><span aria-hidden="true">Pb</span><b>Target</b><small>lead ions in sample</small></div>
          <div class="m-arrow"><span>binds</span>→</div>
          <div class="m-node regulator"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 70" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 51C28 5 42 67 56 18s25 31 33 3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><b>Regulator</b><small>PbrR-inspired switch</small></div>
          <div class="m-arrow"><span>releases</span>→</div>
          <div class="m-node reporter"><i></i><b>Reporter</b><small>visible output</small></div>
        </div>
        <div class="prose mechanism-copy">
          <p>A lead-responsive regulatory element is proposed as the recognition layer. Binding changes transcriptional control, allowing a reporter reaction to produce a visible signal. In a freeze-dried cell-free format, the required biological machinery would be stored in the cartridge and rehydrated by the sample.</p>
          <div class="notice">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3 2.8 20h18.4L12 3Zm0 6v5m0 3h.01" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            <p><strong>Concept status:</strong> this architecture is a literature-informed design direction. AquaSense has not been constructed or experimentally validated.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="cartridge" data-reveal>
        <div class="split">
          <div class="cartridge-visual" role="img" aria-label="Exploded diagram of the cartridge layers">
            <div class="layer layer-1"><span>01</span><b>Sample port</b></div>
            <div class="layer layer-2"><span>02</span><b>Reaction pad</b></div>
            <div class="layer layer-3"><span>03</span><b>Control window</b></div>
            <div class="layer layer-4"><span>04</span><b>Absorbent lock</b></div>
          </div>
          <div class="copy-block">
            <p class="eyebrow">04 · Cartridge</p>
            <h2>Containment you can see.</h2>
            <p class="lead">The enclosure is designed as part of the biosafety strategy, not as packaging added later.</p>
            <p>A one-way sample port would direct water onto a freeze-dried reaction pad. A separate control window would indicate whether the chemistry activated correctly. The absorbent final layer would retain liquid after use, while a tamper-evident seam would discourage reopening.</p>
            <ul class="tag-list" aria-label="Cartridge attributes"><li class="tag">single use</li><li class="tag">no electronics</li><li class="tag">closed reaction</li><li class="tag">control window</li></ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="boundaries" data-reveal>
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">05 · Use boundaries</p>
          <h2>What AquaSense is—and is not.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="boundary-grid">
          <div class="boundary yes"><span>Designed to</span><ul><li>Support preliminary field screening</li><li>Prioritize samples for laboratory testing</li><li>Communicate a simple, bounded next step</li><li>Document uncertainty at the point of use</li></ul></div>
          <div class="boundary no"><span>Not designed to</span><ul><li>Certify that water is safe to drink</li><li>Replace accredited quantitative analysis</li><li>Identify every contaminant in a sample</li><li>Operate without local implementation guidance</li></ul></div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .challenge-map { margin-top: 3rem; padding: 2rem; background: var(--navy); color: #edf9f5; border-radius: var(--radius); overflow-x: auto; }
  .challenge-map > div { min-width: 620px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.2rem 0; }
  .challenge-map > div + div { border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18); }
  .challenge-map .mono { width: 145px; flex: 0 0 auto; color: var(--aqua); }
  .challenge-map b { padding: .6rem .8rem; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.28); border-radius: .6rem; font-size: .8rem; }
  .challenge-map i { flex: 1; min-width: 30px; height: 1px; background: rgba(255,255,255,.28); }
  .requirement-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); overflow: hidden; }
  .requirement { min-height: 260px; padding: 2rem; background: var(--paper-raised); }
  .requirement:nth-child(odd) { border-right: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .requirement:nth-child(n+3) { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .requirement span, .requirement b { font: 500 .68rem 'DM Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .requirement span { color: var(--coral); }
  .requirement h3 { margin: 2.7rem 0 .6rem; }
  .requirement p { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .requirement b { color: var(--aqua-deep); }
  .mechanism-figure { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr; gap: 1rem; align-items: center; margin: 3rem 0; }
  .m-node { min-height: 250px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 1.5rem; text-align: center; background: var(--paper-raised); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); }
  .m-node > span { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 86px; height: 86px; margin-bottom: 1.3rem; background: var(--coral); color: white; border-radius: 50%; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; }
  .m-node svg { width: 100px; height: 86px; margin-bottom: 1.3rem; color: var(--aqua-deep); }
  .m-node.reporter i { width: 86px; height: 86px; margin-bottom: 1.3rem; background: radial-gradient(circle at 35% 30%, #fff2ab, var(--lime) 45%, var(--aqua-deep)); border: 10px solid var(--aqua-pale); border-radius: 50%; }
  .m-node small { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .m-arrow { color: var(--aqua-deep); font-size: 1.7rem; text-align: center; }
  .m-arrow span { display: block; font: .6rem 'DM Mono', monospace; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .mechanism-copy { margin-inline: auto; }
  .cartridge-visual { position: relative; min-height: 560px; perspective: 900px; }
  .layer { position: absolute; left: 8%; width: 84%; height: 120px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-end; padding: 1.1rem 1.4rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 1.2rem; box-shadow: 0 22px 30px rgba(6,47,53,.12); transform: rotateX(58deg) rotateZ(-8deg); }
  .layer span { font: .7rem 'DM Mono', monospace; }
  .layer-1 { top: 2%; background: var(--paper-raised); }
  .layer-2 { top: 21%; background: var(--aqua); }
  .layer-3 { top: 40%; background: var(--lime); color: #062f35; }
  .layer-4 { top: 59%; background: var(--coral); color: white; }
  .boundary-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); overflow: hidden; }
  .boundary { padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); background: var(--paper-raised); }
  .boundary + .boundary { border-left: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .boundary > span { display: inline-block; padding: .35rem .6rem; border-radius: 99px; font: 500 .65rem 'DM Mono', monospace; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .boundary.yes > span { background: var(--aqua-pale); color: var(--aqua-deep); }
  .boundary.no > span { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--coral) 15%, transparent); color: var(--coral); }
  .boundary ul { margin: 2rem 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .boundary li { position: relative; padding: .9rem 0 .9rem 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .boundary li::before { position: absolute; left: .25rem; content: '✓'; color: var(--aqua-deep); font-weight: 800; }
  .boundary.no li::before { content: '×'; color: var(--coral); }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .requirement-grid, .boundary-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .requirement:nth-child(odd) { border-right: 0; }
    .requirement:nth-child(n+2) { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .boundary + .boundary { border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .mechanism-figure { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .m-node { min-height: 190px; }
    .m-arrow { rotate: 90deg; justify-self: center; }
  }
</style>
